      would out-specify the mobile rules and force desktop colors onto the hamburger
      sheet â€” silently discarding `GENERAL_HEADER_DROPDOWN_*_MOBILE`, the exact
      per-instance-setting-discard failure this fix removes at desktop width. So each
      block is scoped to the same breakpoint as the light rule it mirrors, and the
      mobile settings get their own dark-resolved keys.

   Note: the old spike set `border-color` (all sides) on three broad selectors; we set
   only the visible header `border-bottom-color` on `.navbar-static-top.navbar-secondary`
   (the sole authored header border). A cleared source color emits no dark rule (gated,
   matching the light rules). */

/* Unscoped (all widths): the header container + top bar. header.navs is #fff in
