/* Login "or" divider chip. `signup.less` centres an <h4> over a hairline drawn by
   `h4::before`, and punches the hairline out from behind the label by giving the inner
   <span> an opaque `background: #fff` â€” a compile-time literal, so it stays white in dark
   mode. The <h4> sets no color of its own, so it inherits the panel text that the rule
   above flips to --theme-palette-dark: light text on a white chip, 1.00:1, the "or"
   readable only when selected (DIS-3897).

   Take the SAME token the enclosing panel is repainted with â€” the chip's only job is to
   be indistinguishable from the surface it floats over, so any other value re-introduces
   the seam it exists to hide. Every login template puts this inside a Bootstrap panel
   (`.style-editor-panel` on the default, snowflake, reddit and boomi templates; plain
   `.panel.panel-default` on ivanti and asana), and the rule above repaints all of those
